SUMMARY:Going Batty!
DTSTAMP:20260805T111700Z
DTSTART:20260912T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:$37 member / $52 nonmember (per person)Instructor: TBDAges 21+ 
	\n\n\n\nDid you know that bats are the pollinators of the tequila agave? E
	njoy a delicious tequila popsicle as you listen to a local bat expert disc
	uss the important role of bats in our ecosystem as pest control\, seed dis
	persers\, and pollinators. Then go on a bat hike and use special detectors
	 to listen to bat sonar over the Arboretum. \n\n\n\nPlease dress for the w
	eather and wear walking shoes. \n\n\n\n\nregister online\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
	Keep the batty fun going by joining us for our free\, family-friendly Bat 
	Fest on Saturday\, September 27 from 10 am – 2 pm.\n\nhttps://houstonarbor
	etum.org/event/going-batty/\n\nFrom Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/going-batty/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-arboretum
CATEGORIES:Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
